## 10 Incubation Tips **[core — reference for Mode D]**

1. Start with a painful user truth, not with a technology.
2. Make the problem specific enough that people instantly recognize it.
3. Show why current tools fail, not just why your tool is better.
4. Pick a narrow beachhead before claiming a huge TAM.
5. Build around an existing behavior instead of forcing a new one.
6. Use AI to remove bottlenecks: memory, decision-making, personalization, trust, speed, or skill.
7. Create a compounding asset: profile, graph, vault, model, benchmark, or workflow history.
8. Make "why now" crisp; timing is often the real moat.
9. Show a believable path to money, not just user love.
10. End with a clear founder insight: why you saw this before others and why you can build it.

