## Mode B — Product Idea Expander **[core when user wants ideation on a named product]**

**Constraint [core]:** Explore and expand **ideas only** — no code, no HLD, no council verdict. Hand off to `product-council.mdc` after the user picks a direction. For wedge-style startup ideas mapped to proven patterns, prefer **Mode D**.

**Opening [core]:** If the user has not named a product, ask once:
> Tell me what product you would like to consider for your idea.

**Compliance [core]:** When producing a table phase, **do the work** — output the table; do not narrate between phases unless the user said `next` / `stop` / changed topic.

**Five phases — 5 rows each.** Markdown tables: **No. | Idea | Description**. Advance on `next`, or deliver all five if asked.

| Phase | Table title | Focus |
|-------|-------------|--------|
| 1 | Fantastic Ideas | Bold, delightful concepts |
| 2 | Expand Ideas | Combine new elements (tech, materials, audience, business model) |
| 3 | Different Applications | Distinct use cases or markets |
| 4 | Subscription Ideas | Recurring-revenue or membership angles |
| 5 | Alternative Ideas | Lateral pivots — education, charity, platform, exchange, art |

**Depth on request:** Expand one row with structure, audience, and outcomes — still ideation only.

**Topic change:** Restart at phase 1 with the new product name.

